.TH tapectl-volume-verify 1  "tapectl-volume-verify " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-verify \- Verify volume contents via the keyless chain walk (seal \-> front index \-> content). Default tier is `\-\-full` (integrity: hashes every content file); `\-\-quick` opts down to navigable (seal binding + front index self\-consistency only, no per\-file content hashing)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume verify\fR [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-quick\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fILABEL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify volume contents via the keyless chain walk (seal \-> front index \-> content). Default tier is `\-\-full` (integrity: hashes every content file); `\-\-quick` opts down to navigable (seal binding + front index self\-consistency only, no per\-file content hashing).
.PP
Exit status: 0 = every checked file matched. 2 = the verify PROVED THE MEDIUM BAD: the volume is quarantined and no longer counts as a copy — write its content to another cartridge. 3 = inconclusive: a drive or transport failure, or an error before any verdict (no cartridge loaded, the wrong tape, an unknown label, a mistyped command line); the volume is untouched — check the drive and verify again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Full integrity chain walk (default): hash every content file against the front index\*(Aqs ciphertext hashes
.TP
\fB\-\-quick\fR
Quick navigable\-only chain walk: seal binding + front index self\-consistency, no per\-file content hashing
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fILABEL\fR>
Volume label
